  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual request",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'yea, if you could go ahead and explain memes that'd be great!' as the requester of the explanation. The text directly addresses the viewer ('you') in a casual, self-referential manner, inviting the user to imagine themselves in the role of the person asking for clarification. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user is mapped onto the textual request, which is the core action of the meme.",
